    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **65 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured OWNER_CREATED event alongside the existing audit line, in `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the final step of the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**What changed:**\n- Added a static `AtomicLong EVENT_SEQ` that produces a monotonically increasing `seq` across all creates (process-wide, thread-safe).\n- After the existing human-readable audit line, the step now also emits a structured JSON event to the `AUDIT` logger:\n  ```json\n  {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n  ```\n  - `ownerId` = `owner.getId()`\n  - `membershipLevel` = the same derived level shown in the response DTO (`dto.getMembershipLevel()`)\n  - `customerCode` is sourced through a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns the owner's **current** primary identifier.\n\n**Forward-looking design (per the spec's requirement):** the \"current primary identifier\" is deliberately isolated in `primaryIdentifier(Owner)`. Today it returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`; when a later checkpoint unifies the customerCode into the memberId, that one method is the single switch point, so the event will then carry the memberId instead \u2014 without touching the event-rendering logic.\n\nI kept the JSON rendering as a small hand-rolled builder with proper string escaping (rather than pulling in a mapper) since the event shape is fixed and this keeps the step dependency-free and deterministic.\n\nThe new `Cp53Tests` and all 64 other tests pass.",
